[{"page": 1, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-1", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "T9. Cyclodextrin Chemistry", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 150.9783477783203, 271.1499938964844, 172.68597412109375]}, {"text": "7%", "bbox": [290.6499938964844, 193.6215057373047, 304.6280822753906, 207.18873596191406]}, {"text": "9.1", "bbox": [139.8509979248047, 209.5625, 153.9159698486328, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.2", "bbox": [171.47698974609375, 209.5625, 185.54197692871094, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.3", "bbox": [203.10299682617188, 209.5625, 217.16798400878906, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.4", "bbox": [234.72900390625, 209.5625, 248.7939910888672, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.5", "bbox": [266.35498046875, 209.5625, 280.4199523925781, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.6", "bbox": [297.98101806640625, 209.5625, 312.0459899902344, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.7", "bbox": [329.60699462890625, 209.5625, 343.6719665527344, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.8", "bbox": [361.2330017089844, 209.5625, 375.2979736328125, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "9.9", "bbox": [394.06500244140625, 209.5625, 408.1299743652344, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "∑", "bbox": [438.01800537109375, 209.5625, 444.3030090332031, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [144.03500366210938, 225.50250244140625, 149.7313995361328, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "6", "bbox": [175.6610107421875, 225.50250244140625, 181.35740661621094, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "8", "bbox": [207.28700256347656, 225.50250244140625, 212.9833984375, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "3", "bbox": [238.91299438476562, 225.50250244140625, 244.60939025878906, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [270.53900146484375, 225.50250244140625, 276.2353820800781, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [302.16497802734375, 225.50250244140625, 307.8613586425781, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "6", "bbox": [333.7909851074219, 225.50250244140625, 339.48736572265625, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "18", "bbox": [362.5690002441406, 225.50250244140625, 373.9639892578125, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [398.2489929199219, 225.50250244140625, 403.94537353515625, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "53", "bbox": [435.4639892578125, 225.50250244140625, 446.8589782714844, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "Cyclodextrins (CD) are a family of cyclic oligosaccharides, consisting of glucose subunits joined by α-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 244.41796875, 538.5673217773438, 279.00811767578125]}, {"text": "1,4-glycosidic bonds. The three most common cyclodextrins (α-, β-, γ-cyclodextrin) contain 6, 7, and 8", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 271.28851318359375, 538.5916748046875, 284.8557434082031]}, {"text": "α-D-glucopyranoside units, respectively.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 283.2434997558594, 243.17364501953125, 296.81072998046875]}, {"text": "9.1", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 308.853515625, 92.84233856201172, 322.4207458496094]}, {"text": "Calculate the molar mass of β-CD. Assume M𝑤(glucose) = 180.16 g mol−1.", "bbox": [114.69254302978516, 292.2882385253906, 466.0906066894531, 330.1165466308594]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 320.80950927734375, 169.74588012695312, 334.3767395019531]}, {"text": "𝑀𝑤(𝛽−𝐶𝑦𝑐𝑙𝑜𝑑𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑟𝑖𝑛) = 180.16 ⋅7–18.016 ⋅7 = 1135.01g/mol", "bbox": [165.06900024414062, 329.8039855957031, 430.2068786621094, 365.9825744628906]}, {"text": "Mw: β-CD = 1135.01 g/mol", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 362.65252685546875, 238.8031768798828, 376.2197570800781]}, {"text": "2 points", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 376.66949462890625, 152.22015380859375, 390.2367248535156]}, {"text": "2.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 308.77850341796875, 521.8194580078125, 322.3457336425781]}]}, {"page": 2, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-2", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "CDs combine macrocyclic properties with glucose chemistry, which was demonstrated in the synthesis of", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 538.576416015625, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "X. Primary and secondary hydroxy groups show different reactivity due to being a part of CDs. Stoddart", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 167.17449951171875, 538.5524291992188, 180.74172973632812]}, {"text": "et al. synthesised compound K, where only one OH group remained free per glucopyranoside unit.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 179.12950134277344, 516.9561767578125, 192.6967315673828]}, {"text": "equiv.= equivalent", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 361.8929748535156, 142.06114196777344, 396.4831237792969]}, {"text": "9.2", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 399.77349853515625, 92.84233856201172, 413.3407287597656]}, {"text": "Tick the favorable chair conformation and draw the structure of K by complet-", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 399.77349853515625, 480.5821228027344, 413.3407287597656]}, {"text": "ing the CD template. Show stereochemistry unambiguously.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 411.7284851074219, 397.15728759765625, 425.2957458496094]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 423.6835021972656, 169.74588012695312, 437.250732421875]}, {"text": "Since in this reaction we observe the formation of new ring on glucopyranose", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 435.6394958496094, 480.5771179199219, 449.20672607421875]}, {"text": "unit, the bridging atoms should be at axial positions. Therefore, the second", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 447.594482421875, 480.56982421875, 461.1617126464844]}, {"text": "conformation will be favoured.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 459.5494689941406, 258.2328186035156, 473.11669921875]}, {"text": "6 points for correct structure, -2 points for incorrect conformation, -1 point for", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 592.1484985351562, 480.57830810546875, 605.7156982421875]}, {"text": "each incorrect substituent/stereocentre, 0 if no new ring is formed.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 604.103515625, 427.7265319824219, 617.6707153320312]}, {"text": "6.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 399.697509765625, 521.8194580078125, 413.2647399902344]}]}, {"page": 3, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-3", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "9.3", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Determine the ring size, 𝑟𝑠, of macrocycle X. Give the number of stereocentres,", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 151.31396484375, 480.5777893066406, 185.90411376953125]}, {"text": "𝑠𝑐, in X.", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 163.26898193359375, 149.76695251464844, 197.859130859375]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 190.1405029296875, 169.74588012695312, 203.70773315429688]}, {"text": "Cleavage of the diol results in reduction of the number of asymmetric atoms", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 202.0955047607422, 480.57757568359375, 215.66273498535156]}, {"text": "in the glucopyranose unit down to three, one of which (the acetal) is pseudo-", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 214.05050659179688, 480.5652160644531, 227.61773681640625]}, {"text": "chiral.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 226.00550842285156, 143.05519104003906, 239.57273864746094]}, {"text": "Overall, the macrocycle becomes achiral since it consists of meso-", "bbox": [153.76431274414062, 226.00550842285156, 480.5847473144531, 239.57273864746094]}, {"text": "butanetetrol/glycolaldehyde acetal units. The number of atoms in the macro-", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 237.96051025390625, 480.5852966308594, 251.52774047851562]}, {"text": "cyclic ring for each repeat unit is five.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 249.91552734375, 287.7918395996094, 263.4827575683594]}, {"text": "rs: 35", "bbox": [145.30499267578125, 394.36248779296875, 170.97000122070312, 407.9297180175781]}, {"text": "sc: 21", "bbox": [303.614990234375, 394.36248779296875, 329.8290100097656, 407.9297180175781]}, {"text": "rs – 4 points; sc – 4 points; 4 points if sc = 14; 2 points if sc = 3 or 2;", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 421.8175048828125, 423.3529052734375, 435.3847351074219]}, {"text": "8.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}, {"text": "α-Cycloaltrin, a synthetic analogue of α-CD, was synthesised as follows.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 451.5085144042969, 387.7309265136719, 465.07574462890625]}]}, {"page": 4, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-4", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "9.4", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Draw the structure of Y with stereochemistry by completing the CD template.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 166.2294921875, 477.2498474121094, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 178.18450927734375, 169.74588012695312, 191.75173950195312]}, {"text": "Correct structure 3 points.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 407.6925048828125, 243.0797119140625, 421.2597351074219]}, {"text": "Epoxide with opposite configuration is also ac-", "bbox": [252.2745361328125, 407.6925048828125, 480.5752868652344, 421.2597351074219]}, {"text": "cepted; -1 point for any missing or incorrect substituent.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 419.6474914550781, 377.59466552734375, 433.2147216796875]}, {"text": "3.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}]}, {"page": 5, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-5", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "In 2000, Sinay et al. demonstrated that a single protic group (NH and OH) at unit 1 directs the next reduc-", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 538.5855102539062, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "tive debenzylation of a primary OH group to unit 4 in the macrocyclic ring (or to unit 3 if the unit 4 position", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 167.17449951171875, 538.5855712890625, 180.74172973632812]}, {"text": "is not available). This allowed the synthesis of the following β-CD dimer as a mixture of constitutional", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 179.12950134277344, 538.5921020507812, 192.6967315673828]}, {"text": "linkage isomers.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 191.0854949951172, 133.08688354492188, 204.65272521972656]}]}, {"page": 6, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-6", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "9.5", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Draw the structure of L on the β-CD template. Fill in all the boxes.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 166.2294921875, 425.138427734375, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 178.18450927734375, 169.74588012695312, 191.75173950195312]}, {"text": "Correct structure 2 points.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 668.4954833984375, 237.33126831054688, 682.0626831054688]}, {"text": "-1 p for each incorrect substituent", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 680.4505004882812, 273.16448974609375, 694.0177001953125]}, {"text": "0 p if 2 or more incorrect substituents", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 692.405517578125, 290.9991760253906, 705.9727172851562]}, {"text": "2.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}]}, {"page": 7, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-7", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "9.6", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Determine the number of isomers of the β-CD dimer that can form during the", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 166.2294921875, 480.5594482421875, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "synthesis by Sinay et. al.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 178.18450927734375, 225.7979278564453, 191.75173950195312]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 190.1405029296875, 169.74588012695312, 203.70773315429688]}, {"text": "Due to β-CD consisting of seven units and being chiral, two regioisomers are", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 202.0955047607422, 480.5871276855469, 215.66273498535156]}, {"text": "formed in the alkylation reaction (M-4R, M-1R). Therefore, the dimer would", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 214.05050659179688, 480.571533203125, 227.61773681640625]}, {"text": "have three isomers with following connections: 4-4, 1-1, 1-4. (Note 4-1 = 1-4)", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 226.00550842285156, 472.3645324707031, 239.57273864746094]}, {"text": "Correct number of isomers 4 points.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 499.2535095214844, 283.836669921875, 512.8207397460938]}, {"text": "4.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}]}, {"page": 8, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-8", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "To confirm the positions of debenzylation, L was subjected to the “hexo-5-enose degradation” reaction,", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 538.59326171875, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "as shown below. The products were then analysed by mass spectrometry.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 167.17449951171875, 400.94134521484375, 180.74172973632812]}, {"text": "9.7", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 314.8265075683594, 92.84233856201172, 328.39373779296875]}, {"text": "Calculate the 𝑚/𝑧value for the two [M+Na]+ peaks that were observed for the", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 290.0081481933594, 480.5662536621094, 355.9605712890625]}, {"text": "degradation products from L. Use integer values of atomic mass.", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 326.781494140625, 418.6291809082031, 340.3487243652344]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 338.73651123046875, 169.74588012695312, 352.3037414550781]}, {"text": "Since we know the chemical formula for the units, we can calculate molecu-", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 350.6914978027344, 480.5752868652344, 364.25872802734375]}, {"text": "lar weights of the two products. Each product should have one unit 2 (black", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 362.646484375, 480.5592956542969, 376.2137145996094]}, {"text": "sphere) and 2-3 unit 1s (white sphere). Additionally, we should add C2H3O2,", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 374.6014709472656, 480.5781555175781, 388.168701171875]}, {"text": "which corresponds to the mass of the OAc group. Therefore:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 386.5574645996094, 397.82867431640625, 400.12469482421875]}, {"text": "𝑀1 ∶2C27H28O5 + C22H25O4 + C2H3O2 = C78H84O16", "bbox": [120.66899871826172, 399.7421569824219, 366.4583740234375, 465.694580078125]}, {"text": "[𝑀1 + Na]+= 1299", "bbox": [415.47198486328125, 399.7421569824219, 498.51812744140625, 465.694580078125]}, {"text": "𝑀2 ∶3C27H28O5 + C22H25O4 + C2H3O2 = C105H112O21", "bbox": [120.66897583007812, 415.2841491699219, 375.42535400390625, 481.236572265625]}, {"text": "[𝑀2 + Na]+=1731", "bbox": [418.0599670410156, 415.2841491699219, 498.5257873535156, 481.236572265625]}, {"text": "[𝑀1 + Na]+ = 1299", "bbox": [120.66899871826172, 596.5081176757812, 206.3031463623047, 662.4605102539062]}, {"text": "[𝑀2 + Na]+= 1731", "bbox": [315.57098388671875, 596.5081176757812, 398.61614990234375, 662.4605102539062]}, {"text": "Each correct answer 3 points, total – 6 points", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 648.7274780273438, 323.4075012207031, 662.294677734375]}, {"text": "m/z without Na+ 1p each", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 635.8641357421875, 231.74441528320312, 701.8165283203125]}, {"text": "m/z without C2H2O2 1p each", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 647.8201293945312, 250.0114288330078, 713.7725219726562]}, {"text": "6.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 314.75048828125, 521.8194580078125, 328.3177185058594]}, {"text": "Later, Sollogoub et al.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 702.426513671875, 166.61175537109375, 715.9937133789062]}, {"text": "applied the ability of alkenes to direct the debenzylation to the “ortho”-", "bbox": [178.552001953125, 702.426513671875, 538.5833129882812, 715.9937133789062]}, {"text": "glucopyranose unit for the synthesis of hexadifferentiated α-CD S:", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 714.3815307617188, 364.3966064453125, 727.94873046875]}]}, {"page": 9, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "ocr", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [57.0, 67.5, 105.5, 82.0]}, {"text": "AChO Q9-9", "bbox": [57.0, 79.5, 536.5, 130.0]}, {"text": "58th International", "bbox": [57.0, 114.5, 128.0, 120.5]}, {"text": "Chemistry Olympiad", "bbox": [56.5, 123.0, 130.5, 132.0]}, {"text": "Uzbekistan 2026 English (Official)", "bbox": [56.5, 130.0, 535.5, 144.0]}, {"text": "1) (COCI), DMSO o 1) DIBAL-H (1 equiv.)", "bbox": [238.5, 203.5, 401.0, 217.5]}, {"text": "2) (CeHs)3P=CH2 2) MsCl", "bbox": [240.5, 220.0, 379.5, 226.5]}, {"text": "3) NaNs", "bbox": [355.5, 228.0, 380.0, 234.5]}, {"text": "1) DIBAL-H (2 equiv.)", "bbox": [422.0, 251.5, 488.0, 258.0]}, {"text": "2) NaH,", "bbox": [421.0, 261.5, 444.5, 268.0]}, {"text": "ayer", "bbox": [422.5, 271.0, 466.0, 290.5]}, {"text": "he", "bbox": [228.0, 267.5, 233.0, 271.0]}, {"text": "1) CFSCOOH R 1) DIBAL-H (1 equiv.)", "bbox": [251.5, 303.0, 400.5, 317.0]}, {"text": "2) NaH, Bnl 2) Boo0 (1 equiv.)", "bbox": [253.5, 319.0, 397.0, 326.5]}, {"text": "3) DIBAL-H (2 equiv.) 3) MsCl", "bbox": [238.5, 327.5, 379.0, 335.0]}, {"text": "4) NaNa", "bbox": [355.0, 335.5, 380.0, 342.0]}, {"text": "°°", "bbox": [401.0, 361.5, 406.0, 367.0]}, {"text": "kK ke", "bbox": [318.5, 362.5, 417.0, 388.0]}, {"text": "~ Boc,0 = 07 ~o* ~o\" Mscl = Hac So", "bbox": [186.5, 376.0, 416.0, 385.0]}]}, {"page": 10, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-10", "bbox": [377.97100830078125, 59.77293014526367, 538.6260986328125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8270263671875, 128.718505859375, 535.992919921875, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "9.8", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Draw the structures of O-S on the α-CD templates. Fill in all the boxes. You", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 166.2294921875, 480.5919494628906, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "may draw structures outside the boxes if appropriate. Assume 1,2-unit modifi-", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 178.18450927734375, 480.5878601074219, 191.75173950195312]}, {"text": "cation happens clockwise, while 1,3-unit modification happens counterclock-", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 190.1405029296875, 480.5771179199219, 203.70773315429688]}, {"text": "wise. Protic groups have stronger directing effects than alkenes.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 202.0955047607422, 416.9670104980469, 215.66273498535156]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 214.05050659179688, 169.74588012695312, 227.61773681640625]}, {"text": "O - 2 points, P-S - 4 points, total 18 points. -1 point for incorrect or missing sub-", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 736.8455200195312, 480.5889892578125, 750.4127197265625]}, {"text": "stituents for each structure. Mistakes carried over will be ignored if following", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 748.800537109375, 480.5797119140625, 762.3677368164062]}, {"text": "structures fit the functional group direction logic.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 760.7555541992188, 344.46905517578125, 774.32275390625]}, {"text": "18.0 pt", "bbox": [495.1520080566406, 166.15451049804688, 526.921142578125, 179.72174072265625]}]}, {"page": 11, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q9-11", "bbox": [377.97100830078125, 59.77293014526367, 538.6260986328125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8270263671875, 128.718505859375, 535.992919921875, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "9.9", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Determine the number of all possible arrangements of the functional groups", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 166.2294921875, 480.5634460449219, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "on a hexadifferentiated α-CD (assume only the CH2OH groups have been mod-", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 178.18450927734375, 480.56732177734375, 193.9508819580078]}, {"text": "ified).", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 190.1405029296875, 140.66415405273438, 203.70773315429688]}, {"text": "SOLUTION:", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 202.0955047607422, 169.74588012695312, 215.66273498535156]}, {"text": "If we have 6 linear positions for 6 coloured balls, the total number of arrange-", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 214.05050659179688, 480.57525634765625, 227.61773681640625]}, {"text": "ments will be 6! = 720. But in α-CD, positions are in a circle, which makes all", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 226.00550842285156, 480.5955810546875, 239.57273864746094]}, {"text": "arrangements below equal. The correct answer 6!/6 = 120.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 237.96051025390625, 387.3182067871094, 251.52774047851562]}, {"text": "Correct answer 4 points; if the answer 720 or 60– 2 points, if answer 320 - 1", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 333.63250732421875, 480.5851745605469, 347.1997375488281]}, {"text": "point. All other answers - 0.", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 345.5874938964844, 243.08963012695312, 359.15472412109375]}, {"text": "4.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}]}]